Key design decisions:
- Used aes crate instead of OpenSSL for AES-256-ECB (avoids system dependency)
- All SHA-256/512 implemented from scratch matching the C reference byte-for-byte
- Address manipulation uses unsafe for the same byte-level casting the C code does via (unsigned char *)addr
- The global DRBG state uses static mut with unsafe blocks, matching the C global
- Safe Rust used everywhere else (Vec allocations for VLAs, array copies for borrow-checker workarounds)✓ Created checkpoint 1



